{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-20 05:20:48 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-SessionContext] [Project: session_context_research] Found ExecutionContext class with THREE session ID fields: session_id (stable UUID), transport_session_id (unstable from transport), stable_session_id (from agent_sessions table). RouterContextManager.get_or_create_session_id() creates stable session_id from transport_session_id with 3-tier lookup: in-memory cache \u2192 DB lookup \u2192 create new. | confidence=0.95; entry_type=finding; file=shared/execution_context.py; lines=35-50, 62-112; reasoning={\"how\": \"Code inspection of ExecutionContext dataclass and RouterContextManager.get_or_create_session_id method\", \"what\": \"Three session ID fields with different purposes - transport_session_id is unstable, session_id is stable UUID, stable_session_id appears to be a pass-through field from payload\", \"why\": \"Need to understand session ID types and how ExecutionContext manages them\"}; stage=research; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/session_context_research/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-20T05:20:48.693377+00:00_89b740c5", "timestamp": "2026-01-20T05:20:48.693424+00:00"}
