{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-20 05:21:16 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-SessionContext] [Project: session_context_research] Found critical context flow in server.py: For EVERY tool call, derive_session_identity_preview() computes identity_hash from (repo_root, mode, scope_key, agent_key), then backend.get_or_create_agent_session() creates stable_session_id from identity_hash, which is added to context_payload BEFORE build_execution_context(). This stable_session_id becomes exec_context.stable_session_id. | confidence=0.9; entry_type=finding; file=server.py; lines=326-366, 567-602; reasoning={\"how\": \"Traced server.py call_tool logic - identity derivation happens BEFORE build_execution_context, stable_session_id is injected into context_payload\", \"what\": \"derive_session_identity_preview() creates identity from repo_root + mode + scope_key + agent_key, hashes it, looks up/creates stable_session_id in agent_sessions table, adds to context_payload before ExecutionContext is built\", \"why\": \"Need to understand how stable session identity is derived and passed to ExecutionContext\"}; stage=research; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/session_context_research/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-20T05:21:16.664087+00:00_e4bdf162", "timestamp": "2026-01-20T05:21:16.664124+00:00"}
