{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-20 05:21:59 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-SessionContext] [Project: session_context_research] Found append_entry lookup logic in logging_utils.resolve_logging_context(): Line 91 uses session_key = stable_session_id or session_id, then calls backend.get_session_project(session_key) to lookup binding. If DB lookup fails, fallback to state.get_session_project() (line 147). This matches set_project binding key strategy. | confidence=0.95; entry_type=finding; file=shared/logging_utils.py; lines=84-157; reasoning={\"how\": \"Code inspection of logging_utils.py resolve_logging_context function\", \"what\": \"resolve_logging_context uses same key strategy as set_project - stable_session_id with fallback to session_id, calls backend.get_session_project(session_key) for DB lookup, fallback to JSON state\", \"why\": \"Need to understand how append_entry looks up session bindings\"}; stage=research; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/session_context_research/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-20T05:21:59.312047+00:00_383d591b", "timestamp": "2026-01-20T05:21:59.312089+00:00"}
