{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-20 05:23:10 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-SessionContext] [Project: session_context_research] Found the CORRECT implementation in derive_session_identity_preview() line 350: For project mode, scope_key = transport_session_id (stable across tool calls), NOT execution_id! This is the right approach. However, the OLD derive_session_identity() function (line 300) uses execution_id which is WRONG. Need to verify which function is actually being used in server.py call_tool flow. | confidence=0.95; entry_type=finding; file=server.py; lines=326-366; reasoning={\"how\": \"Code inspection of both derivation functions and comparison of scope_key sources\", \"what\": \"Two functions exist - derive_session_identity_preview uses transport_session_id (correct, stable), derive_session_identity uses execution_id (wrong, unstable). Need to trace which one is active in call_tool path\", \"why\": \"Need to understand which session identity derivation function is actually used\"}; stage=research; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/session_context_research/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-20T05:23:10.489560+00:00_e9b4bbf1", "timestamp": "2026-01-20T05:23:10.489596+00:00"}
