{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-20 05:23:24 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-SessionContext] [Project: session_context_research] Confirmed: server.py call_tool DOES use derive_session_identity_preview() (line 567), which correctly uses transport_session_id for scope_key in project mode. The old derive_session_identity() with execution_id appears to be dead code. This means the architecture is CORRECT - stable_session_id should be consistent across tool calls. | confidence=0.98; entry_type=finding; file=server.py; lines=567; reasoning={\"how\": \"Traced actual function call in call_tool implementation\", \"what\": \"server.py call_tool uses derive_session_identity_preview (line 567) which uses transport_session_id for stable scope_key, derive_session_identity appears to be dead code\", \"why\": \"Need to verify which session identity function is actually used in production code path\"}; stage=research; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/session_context_research/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-20T05:23:24.890505+00:00_1b52d44c", "timestamp": "2026-01-20T05:23:24.890539+00:00"}
